      "side": 1,
      "message": "Following up on my earlier reply: we tried the suggested approach (moving the fork-time reset to `register_trace_task_newtask()` and dropping `android_vh_lock_task_fork`), but during integration/debugging we hit practical issues in our loadable vendor module path (trace-event registration / symbol \u0026 ABI constraints differ from the Android vendor-hook model).\nGiven our upcoming merge window and the need to keep risk low after stability validation, we will keep `android_vh_lock_task_fork` in this revision.\nMain reasons:\n1) Stability / safety: avoid cross-framework changes that add risk at this stage.\n2) Different integration models: `trace_task_newtask` is trace-event based; our implementation uses Android vendor hooks from a loadable vendor module.\n3) Extensibility / callsite timing: this hook sits at the tail of `copy_process()` after `user_events_fork()`, matching the task-lifecycle ordering we need for follow-on work (including coordination with memory-management lifecycle concerns).\nGiven the above, we prefer to retain this hook instead of reusing trace_task_newtask as-is. Sorry for the churn on the earlier comment.",
